<task id="051" project="email-communication-intelligence-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Implement shared/group mailbox capture coverage — extend `GraphSubscriptionManager` per the 050 finding (GATED on 050)</title>
    <phase>P5 — FR-15 capture (parallel, spike-first)</phase>
    <gate>after:050</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Extends the capture path (`GraphSubscriptionManager`) to subscribe to shared + M365-group mailboxes under app-only auth — a security-relevant change to what the app can read, scoped by Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy`. Modifies shared `Services/Communication/`; capture is the ingest source for the whole intelligence spine, so a regression breaks everything downstream. BFF-touching: publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification; code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The design decisions were made in the 050 spike; this task implements the sized, specified delta against the existing manager — well-specified execution, not novel design (any residual design decision was escalated in 050).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P5</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies the shared `Services/Communication/GraphSubscriptionManager.cs` capture path; never concurrent with other shared `Services/Communication/` writers. `/conflict-check` before the PR. Gated on 050.</parallel-reason>
    <dependencies>050</dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement shared + M365-group mailbox capture coverage (FR-15) by extending `Services/Communication/GraphSubscriptionManager.cs` **exactly per the 050 spike finding** — the subscription model, the app-only permission model, the Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy` scoping, and the concrete `GraphSubscriptionManager` delta the finding specified. Do NOT re-derive the model here; follow the finding. If the finding's escalation trigger fired (a design decision beyond sizing), that decision MUST be resolved before this task proceeds.

    An email to a shared/group mailbox MUST be captured, then flow through the SAME downstream path as a user-mailbox email — associated (020), triaged (022), and RI-scored — with no forked capture pipeline. Reuse the existing subscription create/renew + notification-handling machinery; add the shared/group enumeration + subscription + the `ApplicationAccessPolicy`-scoped app-only read per the finding.

    Auth is app-only background (ADR-028), least-privilege via `ApplicationAccessPolicy` (scoped to the intended mailboxes, not tenant-wide). Characterization-guard the existing user-mailbox capture: it MUST stay green before + after. Report the operator permission-grant prerequisites the finding identified.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the communication capture layer, authoritative on `GraphSubscriptionManager`, Graph change-notification subscriptions, Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy` least-privilege scoping, and ADR-028 app-only background auth. Implements the 050-sized delta; does not re-decide the model.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `GraphSubscriptionManager` subscribes to shared + M365-group mailboxes per the 050 finding; an email to a shared/group mailbox is captured and flows through the same downstream association + triage + RI path as a user-mailbox email (no forked pipeline). App-only reads are scoped least-privilege via `ApplicationAccessPolicy`. Existing user-mailbox capture is characterization-pinned green. Operator permission-grant prerequisites are documented. Build clean; unit + seam tests (incl. the capture characterization guard) pass; publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      050 sized the work: the subscription model (shared vs group vs user), the app-only permission + `ApplicationAccessPolicy` posture, and the concrete `GraphSubscriptionManager` delta. This task implements that delta. FR-15 acceptance: an email to a shared/group mailbox is captured, associated, and triaged like a user mailbox — so the capture extension must feed the SAME downstream path (the whole point of not forking).

      r1 owns FR-15 (r4 capture is archived). This track is parallel to the intelligence spine but its output (captured shared/group email) is what Success Criterion 8 exercises end-to-end. Characterization-guard the existing user-mailbox capture — a regression here breaks all downstream intelligence.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/GraphSubscriptionManager.cs (EXTEND — add shared/group enumeration + subscription + ApplicationAccessPolicy-scoped app-only read per the 050 finding)</file>
