  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-15">Scope: an email to a shared/group mailbox is captured, associated, and triaged like a user mailbox; capture feeds the SAME downstream path (no forked pipeline).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (gated on 050)">Scope: implement EXACTLY the 050 finding's specified delta + permission model; do NOT re-derive the subscription/permission model; if 050's escalation fired, the decision MUST be resolved first.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: app-only background auth; least-privilege via Exchange `ApplicationAccessPolicy` scoped to the intended mailboxes (NOT tenant-wide); do NOT `new` a credential — inject the central mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04 / ADR-045">Scope: capture is the ingest path — extend it without breaking user-mailbox capture; characterization-guard the existing behavior green before + after; a shared/group capture failure MUST NOT break user-mailbox capture.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Scope: BFF Hygiene — load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state Placement Justification (extends `GraphSubscriptionManager`, no new service, no forked pipeline); publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB (expected ≈0); no new HIGH CVE; update tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` + seam tests (ADR-038).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root §11">Scope: extend the one capture manager — do NOT add a second subscription mechanism / capture pipeline.</constraint>
  </constraints>

