  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the 050 finding (`notes/050-fr15-mailbox-capture-spike.md`) — the subscription model, permission model, `ApplicationAccessPolicy` posture, the concrete `GraphSubscriptionManager` delta, and any escalated decision (must be resolved before proceeding). Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` + ADR-028.</step>
    <step order="2">Characterization guard FIRST: pin the existing user-mailbox capture behavior green as the baseline (NFR-04).</step>
    <step order="3">Read `GraphSubscriptionManager.cs` to identify the existing subscription create/renew + notification-handling seams to reuse.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the delta per the finding: shared/group mailbox enumeration + subscription create/renew + `ApplicationAccessPolicy`-scoped app-only read; reuse the existing notification handling — no forked pipeline.</step>
    <step order="5">Verify captured shared/group email flows through the SAME downstream path (association 020 + triage 022 + RI) as user-mailbox email.</step>
    <step order="6">Write unit + seam tests: (a) a shared-mailbox email is captured + flows downstream (associated + triaged); (b) an M365-group-mailbox email is captured + flows downstream; (c) app-only reads are scoped via `ApplicationAccessPolicy` (least-privilege, not tenant-wide); (d) NEGATIVE — a shared/group capture failure does not break user-mailbox capture (characterization stays green). ADR-038 boundary mocks only.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + targeted `dotnet test`; publish-size (report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB) + CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor gates: `code-review` (focus least-privilege ApplicationAccessPolicy scoping, no forked pipeline, characterization green, app-only auth); `adr-check` against ADR-028 / ADR-045 + spec FR-15 / NFR-04. Address Critical findings; cite Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` capture path).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (051 ✅) + `current-task.md`; document the operator permission-grant prerequisites (from the 050 finding) as an owner-handoff.</step>
  </steps>

